(FIL-93: the file-descriptor tracking table holds up to at least 100000 simultaneously open handles without crashing or reusing a descriptor.
 Also covers: FIL-87, FIL-94.
 The last descriptor is 100002, so none of the 100000 was recycled: every
 one was still open and tracked when the program exited.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-93.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   100002
   100000 opens, none closed, no descriptor reused and nothing crashed
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Write "alpha\nbeta\ngamma\n" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
a number called 'the last descriptor' is 0.
For each attempt from 1 to 100000,
    open a file for reading called handle at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt",
    Set 'the last descriptor' to handle's descriptor.
print 'the last descriptor'.
print "100000 opens, none closed, no descriptor reused and nothing crashed".
